@brunoerg friendly ping for a mutation score and un-killed mutants 🔪 


--- 
I will fix the issues brought up by @DrahtBot soon.

ACK 23cacb13e7

I think having the mempool estimator is a good new functionality that will help to not overestimate the transaction fees.

I only have a non-blocking suggestion: When the mempool estimator fails for whatever reason, I think we could add a new field in the RPC call to inform why the mempool estimator was not choosen. Currently, we save in the `LogDebug` the information of why the mempool estimator failed, but even here it can be difficult to see why the mempool is not healthy (not having enough blocks, block reorg, not having the block weight, or a low representation ratio). I think we could return the reason of why the mempool estimator failed or at least add it to the `LogDebug`. 

<details>
<summary>I implemented a version of how I would return the reason (probably there is a better way to do this):</summary>

